It's tennis.  When both players reach 40 points, it's called deuce.  One player must get two consecutive points to win.  If the server gets the next point, it's called AD IN.  If his service is bad, his opponent gets the point, and it's called AD OUT.

Since the player with the advantage (that is the "AD") must get the next point to win, if the other player gets it, the score goes back to deuce, and it all starts again.

